<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ DMO lifts interest rates on Kiwi Bonds.</title>
<headline>NZ DMO lifts interest rates on Kiwi Bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's Debt Management Office said on Tuesday it had raised the interest rates on its Kiwi Bonds.</p>
<p>For subscriptions of NZ$5,000 to $250,000, the rate on the six-month maturity rose one percent to 7.5 percent, while the one-year rate rose 0.25 percent to 7.0 percent.</p>
<p>The rate on the two and four year maturities fell by 0.25 and 0.5 percent respectively, to 6.75 percent.</p>
<p>The changes were in response to recent changes in wholesale interest rates, the DMO said.</p>
